codex
The last residual revealed a specification framing issue, not a semantic one: loading the module correctly installs the closure, while the destination accidentally required the module scope to remain empty. I’m expressing the theorem at the exact post-load invocation boundary, with the closure’s parameters and body pinned in the scope; this is the contract’s exact-binding form and avoids claiming that loading has no state effect.
apply patch
