The full-configuration rule is compiled but still fails operational matching despite the theorem matching as a circularity. I’m narrowing the issue by restating both theorem and bridge over the semantics’ actual footprint: arbitrary continuation and framed cells, but only the active environment and the three local bindings the loop reads/writes. This is sound because the universal bridge-free theorem will have exactly the same generalized domain.
