codex
Even with the absence guard, the prover explores an impossible cell-frame branch before simplifying map membership. I’m making the local map exact—`a`, `b`, `result`, `x`, `y` only—while retaining arbitrary continuation and all outer-cell frames. That matches every reachable loop head in this function and syntactically eliminates the spurious closure-cell branch.
apply patch
